  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal obligations for NAICS 334511 are $11B for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, allocating $8.9B, followed by the Department of Transportation at $1B and the Department of Homeland Security at $837M. Award activity shows 6,620 contract actions with an average award size of $1.7M. Obligations fell 40.2% year over year. Historical context shows obligations rose from $13.2B in FY21 to $18.4B in FY25 before moving to $11B in FY26 to date. Supplier concentration is visible among a few large vendors: RAYTHEON COMPANY appears multiple times in the top vendor list with awards of $1.6B, $573M, $301M, and $269M, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears with $841M and $302M. Contracting patterns to date concentrate on defense needs, but multiple civilian agencies also appear among the top buyers. All figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
